all that a large  dope bust this is none of those things  this is war and what we said if you can  take the psychedelic and political  struggles of the 1960s and boil it down  into one phrase what did we stand for we  stood for making love not war  [Applause]  and ever since Thomas the Marines were  shoved into the sea at Da Nang and the  CIA was helicoptered off the embassy  roof in Saigon we've been able to hold a  delicate and very tense balance between  the view of the dominator weapon  worshiping old-style macho approach to  things and our own and I think we all  felt I certainly did last August when  they began to move the chess pieces  around that we would not stand for it  that there was a we and that we would  not stand for it  and if you were able to keep your  idealism intact until the congressional  debate when you felt then they represent  us they will stop it after all it's the  opposition party to the administration  it's an anti-war party they will stop it  and they went like sheep to the  slaughter to the slaughter and they  voted for it so now we have no excuse no  no faction was overridden  nobody's rights were trampled on the  path to this debacle we we the people of  the United States by some staggering  percentage approve of this well so  that's to people like myself and Tim  Leary and Bob Wilson and John Lilly and  all the people who aren't here and all  of you that I've grown up with and  worked with this is an abomination we  stand for consciousness expansion do you  know how much you have to have for  brains to wage war its staggers the  imagination  we stood for deconditioning asking  questions resisting Authority today no  questions are being asked  authority is not being resisted oh yes  there are demonstrations against the war  but in a democracy they have what's  called a 5% rule it doesn't matter if  only five percent are involved in it it  doesn't matter what it is so we have  been effectively isolated our names are  have been metaphorically signed to the  bottom line of these documents that  commits us to war how do you feel about  that
 

